@startuml remote-workplace-attach
!theme plain
title Remote workplace (v1.3): the remote harness attaches by SSH into its own OS user on our host; tool calls run inside that boundary; tasks arrive through the mailbox; no commands flow towards the remote machine

participant "Remote harness\n(model on the remote side)" as RH
participant "SSH daemon\n(our host)" as SSHD
participant "Remote workplace\n(OS user ext_k: home, firewall)" as WP
participant "rwh tool runner\n(inside ext_k)" as RW
participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Bridge\n(broker, mailbox)" as BR
participant "Task core (board)" as B
database "Carrier" as MX

== attach (connection towards our host only) ==
RH -> SSHD: ssh ext_k@host, key K (pinned in authorized_keys);\nhost key fingerprint checked against the credential package
SSHD -> WP: session as uid ext_k; forced command: rwh tool runner
WP -> RW: start inside the user boundary\n(firewall: only broker + egress proxy; no other egress)
RW --> RH: tool channel open (framed over the SSH session)
note right of RW
  Only tool execution crosses this channel.
  Our side never opens a connection to the
  remote machine and never sends commands into it.
end note

== task ==
O -> B: snapshot of the task for K (projection of one element)
O -> BR: signed message to K: "task X, snapshot ref" (grant: session.input? no — post to K's mailbox)
BR -> BR: verify signature, grant, decision guard; mailbox record
BR -> MX: doorbell to K's identity
RH -> BR: mailbox read (through its tool, over the carrier) → body + verification record
RH -> RH: agent loop decides to take the task

== work ==
loop tool calls
  RH -> RW: tool call (bash, git, files) over the SSH channel
  RW -> WP: execute as ext_k; egress only through the profile proxy
  RW --> RH: result
end
RH -> BR: post result (signed by K); audience projection → thread
BR -> B: outcome proposal for the element

== retire ==
O -> O: revoke K's workplace (grant user.create)
note right of O: archive home, remove authorized_keys,\ndelete user ext_k, remove firewall rules;\nK's identity stays pinned unless revoked
@enduml
